---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Acceptable Use Policy - BodhicAI">
    <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding: var(--space-2xl) 0;">
        <h1 style="font-size: clamp(24px, 5vw, 36px); margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);">Acceptable Use Policy</h1>
        <div style="color: var(--body); line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px;">
            <p>Last updated: August 6, 2026</p>
            <p>This Acceptable Use Policy ("AUP") outlines the rules and guidelines for using the BodhicAI marketplace. By accessing or using our platform, you agree to comply with this policy. Violations may result in Content removal, account suspension, or permanent termination.</p>

            <h3 style="color: var(--ink); margin-top: var(--space-xl);">1. Prohibited Content</h3>
            <p>You may not upload, publish, or distribute Content that:</p>
            <ul style="margin-left: var(--space-lg); margin-top: var(--space-sm);">
                <li><strong>Contains Malware:</strong> Any code designed to damage, disrupt, or gain unauthorized access to computer systems, networks, or user devices.</li>
                <li><strong>Includes Prompt Injections:</strong> Instructions designed to manipulate, bypass, or override AI safety mechanisms, system prompts, or content moderation filters.</li>
                <li><strong>Facilitates Illegal Activity:</strong> Content that aids in hacking, phishing, fraud, identity theft, money laundering, or any other unlawful activity.</li>
                <li><strong>Infringes Intellectual Property:</strong> Plagiarized content, unauthorized copies of proprietary code, or Content that violates copyrights, patents, or trademarks.</li>
                <li><strong>Contains Harmful or Abusive Material:</strong> Content promoting violence, hate speech, harassment, discrimination, or exploitation of any kind.</li>
                <li><strong>Is Misleading or Deceptive:</strong> False claims about functionality, fake reviews, manipulated metrics, or exaggerated marketing descriptions.</li>
                <li><strong>Violates Privacy:</strong> Content that collects, stores, or transmits personal data without consent, or exposes private information of individuals.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 style="color: var(--ink); margin-top: var(--space-xl);">2. Prohibited Behaviors</h3>
            <p>Users of BodhicAI must not:</p>
            <ul style="margin-left: var(--space-lg); margin-top: var(--space-sm);">
                <li>Create multiple accounts to circumvent bans, manipulate reviews, or artificially inflate metrics.</li>
                <li>Engage in fraudulent transactions, including fake purchases or chargebacks intended to defraud creators.</li>
                <li>Scrape, crawl, or use automated tools to extract Content or data from the platform without authorization.</li>
                <li>Attempt to reverse-engineer, decompile, or tamper with the platform's infrastructure or security systems.</li>
                <li>Harass, threaten, or abuse other users, creators, or BodhicAI staff through any communication channel.</li>
                <li>Resell or redistribute purchased Content without the explicit permission of the original creator.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 style="color: var(--ink); margin-top: var(--space-xl);">3. Security Requirements for Creators</h3>
            <p>All Content uploaded by Creators must pass our automated security scanning process. Specifically:</p>
            <ul style="margin-left: var(--space-lg); margin-top: var(--space-sm);">
                <li>Content must not contain embedded scripts that execute without user awareness.</li>
                <li>API keys, secrets, or credentials must never be included in uploaded Content.</li>
                <li>Content must not attempt to exfiltrate data from user systems.</li>
                <li>Any external dependencies or API calls must be clearly documented in the Content description.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 style="color: var(--ink); margin-top: var(--space-xl);">4. Bounty System Rules</h3>
            <p>When participating in the Bounty system:</p>
            <ul style="margin-left: var(--space-lg); margin-top: var(--space-sm);">
                <li>Bounty posters must provide clear, achievable requirements.</li>
                <li>Bounty claimers must deliver original work that meets the stated requirements.</li>
                <li>Submitting pre-existing or recycled Content to claim bounties is prohibited.</li>
                <li>Payment disputes will be mediated by BodhicAI in accordance with our dispute resolution process.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 style="color: var(--ink); margin-top: var(--space-xl);">5. Enforcement</h3>
            <p>BodhicAI enforces this policy through a combination of automated scanning, community reporting, and manual review. Violations are addressed as follows:</p>
            <ul style="margin-left: var(--space-lg); margin-top: var(--space-sm);">
                <li><strong>First Violation:</strong> Warning and Content removal.</li>
                <li><strong>Second Violation:</strong> Temporary account suspension (7–30 days).</li>
                <li><strong>Severe or Repeated Violations:</strong> Permanent account termination and forfeiture of pending payouts.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>BodhicAI reserves the right to bypass the graduated enforcement process for severe violations that pose immediate risk to users or the platform.</p>

            <h3 style="color: var(--ink); margin-top: var(--space-xl);">6. Reporting Violations</h3>
            <p>If you encounter Content or behavior that violates this policy, please report it to us at <a href="mailto:support@bodhicai.tech" style="color: var(--primary);">support@bodhicai.tech</a> with the subject line "AUP Violation Report." Include the relevant Content URL and a description of the violation.</p>

            <h3 style="color: var(--ink); margin-top: var(--space-xl);">7. Changes to This Policy</h3>
            <p>BodhicAI may update this Acceptable Use Policy at any time. Material changes will be communicated via email or platform notification. Continued use of the platform constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</Layout>
